S1-UIX-05: Usability Review & Fix List (Sprint 1)

Task ID: S1-UIX-05  
Role: UI/UX Designer  
Scope: Design Compliance & Usability Audit of Built Screens vs. Student Guide Specs & Hi-Fi Mockups  

1. Design System & Accessibility Audit

-Color Tokens & Contrast: Primary Teal 700 (`#0B6E64`) and Accent Coral 700 (`#C9432C`) pass WCAG AA contrast standards against light backgrounds (`#FFFFFF`, `#DDF1EE`).
-Typography Scale: Verified visual hierarchy across Display (Sora 700 / 40px), Headings (Sora 600 / 24px), and Body (DM Sans 400 / 16px).
-Form Controls: Input focus states correctly display a teal border highlight with soft focus ring.

 2. Developer Audit & Fix List

Fix Item 1: Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) & System Security
-Audit Finding (§1.2 & §3.8): Admins can manage standard Users only; Superadmin accounts must remain hidden from Admin views.
-Developer Requirement:
-Ensure Superadmin accounts do not show up in the User Management list when an Admin is logged in.
-Hiding action buttons in the front-end is a courtesy; the backend server MUST enforce role checks on every API request.

Fix Item 2: Soft Delete, Status Badges & Stamp Audit
-Audit Finding (§2.3): Soft-deleted rows (`status = Inactive`) must remain in the database to prevent breaking foreign keys (e.g., sales referencing deleted customers).
-Developer Requirement:
  -Admin / Superadmin View: Show all rows (Active and Inactive). Inactive rows must be shaded with a red `Inactive` badge (`#B42318`), direct Audit Stamp text, and a **Restore** button replacing Edit/Delete.
  -User View: Filter out `status = Inactive` rows on the backend (`WHERE status = 'Active'`). Hide the **Status** and **Stamp** columns completely from standard User accounts.

Fix Item 3: Navigation & Active Route Indicator
-Audit Finding (§3.2): Active sidebar navigation states.
-Developer Requirement: Active sidebar links must feature background fill `#DDF1EE` with icon/text colored `#0B6E64`. Modules restricted by an Admin must be greyed out or removed from the menu.

Sign-Off Criteria
- Database audit stamp tracks latest action (`CREATED`, `EDITED`, `DELETED`), user, and timestamp.
- Responsive container layouts conform strictly to Sprint 1 mockups.
